h('Appendix C Reproducibility and research integrity',True)
h('C.1 Input identity and scope of the revised analysis')
paras('The new analysis uses gemini.zip, llama_seed_0_results.zip, llama_seed_42_results.zip and llama_seed_123_results.zip as its sole inference-result sources. The project archive supplies taxonomy files and scoring/generation code; historical response roots are not pooled into the revised metrics. input_manifest.json records SHA-256 hashes of the four result archives. The original reviewed PDF and its comments remain the record of requested revisions.',
'The alignment audit checks entity identifiers, gold metadata and main prompt text across model runs. It finds no main-prompt or gold-list mismatch across the three Llama seeds and Gemini. All 37,353 scheduled response records identify Rod Fergusson as the external demonstration and set demonstration_omitted to false. Completion and validity are audited independently of metric outcomes.',
'The source code implementing the recomputation, the exact nine prompt examples, condition summaries, paired comparisons, seed summaries, entity inventory, non-gold label occurrences, attempt audit and failure sensitivity accompany this draft. Unrounded numerical values are retained. SHA-256 input fingerprints identify the actual archived result sets rather than only a directory name.')
h('C.2 Reproduction procedure and retained provenance')
for t in ['1. Place the four result archives in upload/ with their recorded filenames. Extract the relevant taxonomy data and original scorer from the project archive into project_source/thesis/archive/original/.', '2. Run analysis/recompute.py to load the new responses, verify context extraction, calculate entity-level scores and derive paired comparisons. Required libraries are NumPy, pandas and NetworkX.', '3. Run analysis/audit_extra.py to verify prompt alignment, deduplicate attempt records, calculate first-attempt validity and produce failure-sensitivity bounds.', '4. Run analysis/build_revision.py to regenerate the manuscript tables, figures and PDF. Rendering uses Matplotlib and ReportLab with DejaVu fonts; analysis/finalize_pdf.py adds the page-numbered contents and navigation bookmarks using PyMuPDF.', '5. Inspect the rendered pages and retain the input archives, scripts, numerical tables and manuscript together. A new inference run should use a separate result root and preserve unsuccessful attempts.']:p(t)
paras('The re-analysis makes no new model API calls. It evaluates retained responses and their recorded prompts. Supplementary cache files are temporary conveniences and are excluded from the deliverable package; the raw result archives remain the primary evidence. Failure counts are not hidden by labelling every scheduled response completed, and partially generated lists are not silently converted into successful answers.',
'The precision of a printed decimal is not a claim that model behaviour is known to four decimal places. Four-place labels permit exact comparison of rounded table entries; uncertainty and reproducibility depend on the paired cohorts, seeds, input data and protocol. The analysis retains these distinctions throughout.')
h('C.3 Attribution, assistance and author review')
paras('The dataset and taxonomy are attributed to the WiKC authors; the original knowledge base is attributed to Wikidata. Prompting methods and evaluation concepts are cited at their points of use. The author’s exploratory development account is explicitly distinguished from completed controlled experiments. Qualitative error interpretations are not represented as independent human annotation.',
'Generative AI assisted this revision through manuscript drafting and restructuring, literature lookup, analysis-code preparation, numerical recomputation, figure generation and document formatting. The evaluated Gemini and Llama outputs are experimental data and are distinguished from AI assistance used to prepare the manuscript. Responsibility for checking the analysis, citations, interpretations and final submission remains with the thesis author.',
'This appendix is a transparent methods-and-assistance disclosure, not a signed declaration of independent work or a certification that institutional requirements have been satisfied. Any institutionally prescribed declaration must use the approved wording and be reviewed and signed by the author. Primary records should be retained in accordance with the applicable research-integrity requirements. The manuscript does not assert that an independent semantic audit has been completed.')
